WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.529
Good morning, John. Ten years ago today,
I know exactly where I was…

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:08.540
because I was inside a Target for 15 hours…

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:09.940
Ten years ago!

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.300
The last ten years have been really big. It’s been big -
and I can’t really talk - like, get my mind around it even.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.060
But I do know that I have changed a lot and
what we do on this channel has changed a lot.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.499
For example, in order to prepare for this
video, I went to look at my schedule for 2010

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.860
and discovered that I didn’t have a schedule
in 2010!

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.460
But I think more importantly than that, over the last
ten years, John, you and I have gotten less interested

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.600
in optimizing this channel for growth for
like reaching new audience.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:42.510
If you find your way here, absolutely good work.
But we’re not really trying to grow it, for three reasons.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.990
One, it’s just gotten harder
and our skills are less suited to it.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:49.260
Two, YouTube recommends stuff
based on lots of different things.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.220
Specifically, it would like us to make
8 to 12 minute long Vlogbrothers videos,

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.900
and I just don’t want to!

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.530
I like this! I like making 4 minute videos,
and that’s the rules!

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:04.600
But most importantly number 3: growth, beyond a
certain point, just gets less interesting... and worse?

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.820
Depending on what you want to do, of course,
but like specifically for this channel.

00:01:07.829 --> 00:01:12.890
Let’s talk about why. But first, 
how many nails does a carpenter need?

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:16.100
It depends on what they’re building, right?
So you have to look and say, “What do I wanna do?”

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.880
And obviously for any given project,
it’s bad to have not enough nails.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.880
But after a certain point, 
you can have too many nails.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.700
Eventually you have so many nails that
the nails don't provide you relief from stress.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.600
They ADD to your stress.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.979
The point is to get to HERE.

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:35.560
Eventually you just spend more time thinking about
your nails than you do actually building a house.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.920
I’ve thought about this a lot
in the last couple weeks.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.880
I just don’t think that at its core, 
Vlogbrothers is about entertainment.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.320
Yes, I want to do that sometimes.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:47.549
But I think it’s about doing things together
and thinking about things together.

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:51.300
Things like Life’s Library and the Project for
Awesome and our work with Partners in Health

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.600
and just all of the ideas that 
we’ve talked about over the years

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.729
that have helped me understand how to be a
person and how the world works.

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:00.149
And Dear Hank and John
and SciShow and Crash Course.

00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:05.440
SciShow and Crash Course long ago eclipsed
Vlogbrothers in subscribers, in views, all that stuff.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.100
But Vlogbrothers, just by virtue of the fact
that those channels wouldn’t exist without it,

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:13.500
has had more impact on the world
despite having a smaller audience.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.879
Sometime in the last ten years, and not all
at once, and not at the same time,

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.140
John and I realized that you don’t need
a million nails to build a house.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.080
We actually internalized this - it took awhile -
that this channel isn’t about

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.980
having the biggest number under the video.
It’s about doing things, creating stuff,

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.520
thinking about things together.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.080
And not only is that like a goal of mine;
it’s also when I’m most happy.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.849
And there are limits to that, because I want
it to actually be a group of people

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:45.970
who recognize the humanity of all of the other people.
And as the numbers get too big, you lose track of that.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.460
Also, this channel is unquestioningly personality-based.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:54.040
And having too many people have opinions about
your personality, it turns out, is not great, actually.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.720
Crash Course now has over ten million subscribers,
and it should grow as much as it can,

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:02.010
because its goal is to reach people
with educational content.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.740
But Vlogbrothers?
Like no, we’re good.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:10.060
You, watching this video, are part of something
that helps stuff exist in the world.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.320
And that stuff is sometimes real stuff.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:18.400
Sometimes it’s ideas that we wouldn’t have
if we weren’t thinking together as a community.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:23.820
That’s pretty weird and it’s cool and it's special
and I’m really, really happy about it.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.319
And in that vein, three things.

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:29.470
First, the Nerdfighteria Census is out!
You can go fill it out right now.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.300
Thank you so much to people who do that so
that we can understand who we all are better.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.200
We’ve been doing the census
every year since 2013,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.790
and it’s super vital to how we make decisions
about what we do.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:43.080
So if you can take the 10 to 20 minutes it will take
to fill it out, please please please do so.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.580
Number two, the Kindle ebook of An Absolutely
Remarkable Thing is 3 bucks right now.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:50.680
So if you want to get it dirt cheap, you can.
I don’t think it’s gonna be that way for much longer.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:54.240
And finally, if you want to come see us in
Atlanta or Raleigh or St. Pete next week,

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.240
we will be there.
John, I’ll see you on Tuesday.

